Expose add_many on the DatabaseLoginsStorage wrapper

Upstream version skew inside the Firefox 153 tree, not a LibreWolf divergence.

  mobile/android/android-components/.../SyncableLoginsStorage.kt:211-213 calls
  getStorage().addMany(asEntries) on the DatabaseLoginsStorage WRAPPER, and
  components/lib/passwords-file/.../CsvPasswordsFileImporter.kt:64 does the same.

  third_party/application-services/components/logins/src/logins.udl:182 declares
  `sequence<BulkResultEntry> add_many(sequence<LoginEntry> logins);` so uniffi does
  generate LoginStore.addMany(). But the hand-written wrapper at
  DatabaseLoginsStorage.kt only re-exports add / update / addOrUpdate /
  findLoginToUpdate -- never addMany -- at the revision moz.yaml pins
  (06c391e81c367d1059d601c812f379875d7ef0a3, 2026-05-13).

  Result: `Unresolved reference 'addMany'` and the Fenix Gradle stage fails.

WHY MOZILLA DOES NOT HIT THIS: their Android builds consume a PREBUILT
application-services artifact, built from a revision that matches
android-components. LibreWolf builds it from source
(--enable-appservices-in-tree, LW-M2-05) precisely so the search-config dumps and
the Rust components are ours to control -- and that is what exposes the skew. So
this patch is a cost of in-tree appservices, and it must be re-checked on every
rebase: if a later revision adds the wrapper method, this patch will reject
loudly, which is the desired behaviour.

The wrapper mirrors the file's existing delegation style exactly (@Throws +
one-line `return store.<method>(...)`), so it carries no LibreWolf behaviour --
it only restores a method the UDL already promises.

Found by the skeptical verification of LW-M2-04, which discovered the APK had been
built with this fix applied as an UNCOMMITTED local edit that existed in no patch,
making the deliverable irreproducible.
---
--- a/third_party/application-services/components/logins/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/logins/DatabaseLoginsStorage.kt
+++ b/third_party/application-services/components/logins/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/logins/DatabaseLoginsStorage.kt
@@ -105,6 +105,11 @@
         return store.addOrUpdate(entry)
     }
 
+    @Throws(LoginsApiException::class)
+    fun addMany(entries: List<LoginEntry>): List<BulkResultEntry> {
+        return store.addMany(entries)
+    }
+
     fun registerWithSyncManager() {
         return store.registerWithSyncManager()
     }
